WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:01.160
"Hey!"

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.200
I

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.100
Didn't think we could make another episode

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.700
But

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:05.640
We did it

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.940
A lot of these are thanks to you guys

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:08.920
Number 1

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.780
So we know that you can shortcut to your first item quickslot by holding down on the D-Pad

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.180
But did you know

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.920
That you can also shortcut to your first attune spell

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.080
by holding up?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.020
Pure spell caster builds

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.020
have always had it tough

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.020
with toggling between spells.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.020
And the highest skill cap thing

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.020
you can do as a caster, really

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.020
is quickly switch between spells

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.020
to confuse your opponents.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.020
So this gives you more control.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.020
Does this make sorcery viable in PVP?

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.060
No, no it doesn't.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.060
Nothing will.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.060
Number two is in the running

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.060
for the most obscure secret of Dark Souls 3.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.060
So summon an NPC phantom

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.060
called Swamp Cuculus

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.060
outside of the Old Demon king

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.060
boss fog. And then kill

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.000
the Old Demon King with Cuculus still alive.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Then have an epiphany about

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
how Cuculus is obviously

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Cornyx's apprentice

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.500
And remember to check back att Cornyx's cage in the undead settlement

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.080
A corpse will now be there, holding Cornyx's amazing pyromancy set

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.240
And the spotted whip which poisons foes

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.860
If you found this naturally in your playthrough, well done.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.300
This isn't all you can get from summoning NPC's though.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:26.340
If Knightslayer Tsorig kills you and be honest, I mean he killed everyone right?

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.580
You get the "My thanks!" emote.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.280
If you summon the Londor Pale Shade, you get the "Duel bow",

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.880
if you summon Black Hand Gothard, you get "By my sword",

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.640
and Yellowfinger gives you the "Proper bow".

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.220
I'm quite sure that there's others that I'm missing

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.580
and maybe even some that no one has discovered yet.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.240
I don't know, if you find any let everyone know.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:48.800
Number 3,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.180
New Game Plus is disappointing

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.260
in this game.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.020
Enemy damage doesn't seem to scale too much, and

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.380
I personally haven't noticed any

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.740
new enemy placements,

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.660
which at least Dark Souls II did right.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:01.740
At any rate,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.000
New Game Plus One and New Game Plus Two

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.240
grant access to some of the Plus One and Plus Two, and

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.040
Plus Three rings.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.960
Some of the best ones are

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.900
the Plus Two Gold Serpent Ring,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.660
or the Plus Two Ring of Favour.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.820
I'll leave a list of them all in the description

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.380
if you want to hunt them down.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.480
Number four,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.000
so,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.120
in the last episode,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.800
I was really surprised to hear

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.740
that so many of you stuck in a Hollowing state

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.320
without a way to cure it.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.380
I just realised that

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.920
it sounds like I'm making fun of you,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.760
but it really is really hard

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.060
to cure Hollowing if you don't know how.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:36.760
So,

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.800
if you don't have access to purging stones

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.500
because Yuria has gone,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.660
then just go to the Statue of Velka,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.560
after purchasing the Grave Key

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.800
and you can request

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.080
dissolution there.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.520
Once you've done this and

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.480
healed the Dark Sigil at the Firekeeper,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.220
then,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:52.800
you know,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.240
all those hours spent in the character creator,

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.860
they were no longer for nothing.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.100
Number five,

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.740
the Hollow Gem Infusion allows a weapon to scale with your Luck stat,

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.980
which I'm discovering is

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.600
awesome if you run a Poison or Bleed build,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.340
since those things scale with luck as well

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.420
In addition, though,

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.760
did you know actually that actually being Hollow

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.320
while also having a Hollow Infusion

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.200
gives you a plus five bonus to your Luck stat?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.940
So, if you're running a Luck build,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.540
just infuse your shield with Hollowing, and

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.100
even if it's on your back,

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.660
you're still reaping the benefits.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.040
It's a neat little mechanic to make Luck that

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.680
tiny bit more viable.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.440
Speaking of infusions,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.380
the Simple Infusion also has a hidden benefit.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.700
It scales with Intelligence,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.720
but it also restores focus

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.120
At a rate of about one Focus point

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.660
per four seconds.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.100
Now, that sounds horrible,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:43.700
but

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.740
it is actually amazing for some weapons

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.440
that can take advantage of it

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.800
Take the Sunlight Straight Sword, for example.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.820
If I have zero focus points,

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.760
then I can't cast the buff,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.320
but if I have even one Focus point,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.500
then I can

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.080
So, if you're using a weapon

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.900
that benefits greatly from

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.420
even a tiny amount of Focus, and

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.340
most do,

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:04.980
then

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.140
throw this infusion on an off-hand shield

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.620
or something, it's amazing.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.740
Number seven is to do with consuming Souls.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.900
If you have a ton that you want to consume,

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.180
then the fastest way

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.520
is just to sell them at the Handmaiden.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.180
She gives you the same amount that you'd usually get.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.100
Number eight,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.080
when you're deciding whether to make that risky jump

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.820
because there's a shiny over there;

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.920
consider this,

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.160
important items like Estus Shards

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.920
or weapons or rings,

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.360
they have a large glow,

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.100
whereas regular items, like

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.400
consumables have a small glow.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.580
So, if you have to choose between two items,

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.800
and a giant is about to smack the shit out of you,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.300
then

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.880
make sure you choose the right one.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.000
Number nine,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.940
segway.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.960
So, if you're like me right now

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.280
and you have a huge pile of souls to get back to, then

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.100
never fear

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.420
because here's a mechanic

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.980
I only learned about recently,

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.740
the Ring of Sacrifice makes it so that

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.720
that you don't lose Souls upon death,

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:00.040
which everybody knows,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.340
but did you also know

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.320
that it gives you another chance to recover any lost Souls

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.560
already waiting for you in the world?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:07.680
So, here,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.540
you can see my Souls over there.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.960
I'm going to recover them,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.580
but I die on my way,

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.120
but

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.360
since I have the Ring of Sacrifice equipped,

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.080
the pile of Souls remains,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.820
and I have another chance to recover them.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.320
So, props to Supermandrew Seven

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.120
for making me aware of this one.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.460
Number ten,

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.240
the Giant Tree by your shrine

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.680
it sometimes leaves a Seed of a Giant Tree behind,

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.040
which can be used used to temporarily seed your world.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.300
Any invader into a seeded world,

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.060
will not only have to deal with the host,

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.180
they also have to deal with the normal enemies in that world,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.420
which just, you know, pushes the odds

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.420
more into the host's favor.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.780
I really don't get what From has against invaders.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:50.420
Anyway,

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.020
the trigger for the Seed to drop

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:55.420
appears to be really similar to what it was in Dark Souls II,

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.200
where simply being invaded

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.560
can give you a chance to receive a Seed.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.480
For me, I found it was about a fifty percent chance

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.860
that the seed would appear

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:04.820
after I was invaded,

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.320
but

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.120
my sample size was pretty small,

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.340
so it's hard to say the exact percent.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.320
In Dark Souls II, it was twenty-five percent I believe.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.180
Regardless,

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.480
if you do get invdaded,

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.920
then remember to check for a Seed

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.300
because you an hold up to five at a time

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.440
but only one can be at the tree

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.460
at any one time.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.500
Number eleven,

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.440
if you want to be invaded more often,

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.520
and who doesn't?

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.060
Use a Dried Finger from the Handmaiden

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.180
Using it resets your invasion timer,

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.220
which is nothing new,

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.400
but what is new

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.180
is that it allows you to summon

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.740
a third friendly phantom

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.080
and a second

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.320
invading phantom

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.980
A hidden things is that to remove this effect,

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.220
you have to travel to a new bonfire,

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.860
not just rest at one.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.500
When you get grabbed by the Rock Stray Demon,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.620
did you know that you can mash the shoulder buttons

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:50.860
and the face buttons

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.140
to escape its grab?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.200
Of course you did, you're a Souls veteran

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.420
and you probably do mash a lot of buttons out of reflex,

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:58.440
but in this game,

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.040
the only grab attack I've managed to escape from

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.460
is this one.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.960
Mashing is no use against Mimics,

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.040
the Groos,

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.200
other bosses seem to have a set animation.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.720
I guess the rule is that

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.320
if there's an enemy that sort of

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.980
crushes you and you can see your character

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:17.480
wriggle in response to your button presses, then

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.820
that is when you mash the buttons.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.280
Thirteen,

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.080
the messaging system no longer requires an Orange Soapstone,

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.920
and it's available here in your options menu,

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.220
and at first glance, the messaging system looks terrible

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.420
but that's only until you press the triangle button,

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.140
and

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:35.920
all of a sudden,

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.000
you'll have access to conjugations,

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.480
another extension of your message, and

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.080
even gestures as well,

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.800
which returns from Bloodborne.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.760
Perfect.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.740
If a player rates that message,

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.260
positive or negative,

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.420
I'll receive a health boost,

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.500
at that moment,

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.720
but it is easy funny that it rewards you for

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:00.500
placing a terrible or evil message as well.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:04.160
Number fourteen is a returning mechanic from Dark Souls I

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.340
It's that there's an easy way to deal with Mimics, and

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.600
there are a shitload of Mimics in this game.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.960
Of course, you all know

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.500
that you can tell if it's a Mimic

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.360
if the chain on the side is straight, and

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.320
if the chest itself is very lightly breathing.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.860
Just like in Dark Souls I as well, though

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.480
Lloyd's Talismans put Mimics to sleep

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.620
While asleep,

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.580
they'll allow you to pick up the item it usually drops,

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:34.220
so you can continue on your way after that.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.340
If you're lucky, though,

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.320
it'll drop the Symbol of Avarice,

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.920
which is a helmet that helps you get

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:39.940
more item discovery

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.760
which is great in this game.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.280
The best way to farm this

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.780
is actually just to peg* Lloyd's Talisman at it

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:46.920
until it drops it.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.860
Throw a Talisman,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.220
hit the Mimic to wake it up,

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.920
and then throw another Talisman

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.200
until you get it

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.640
or until you run out of Lloyd's Talismans

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.400
You get more Lloyd's Talismans

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.660
from the Handmaiden

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:58.780
after picking up

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.420
the Paladin's ashes.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.480
Kudos to Pitara* on Reddit

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.680
for reminding me that

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.580
Lloyd's Talismans are a thing.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.020
Alright, so this last thing

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.380
isn't just a discovery, it's

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.280
also a bit of a call to action,

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.720
which I haven't done very often,

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.360
so I'm interested to see how well this can work.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:16.120
So

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.640
I can't quite figure out this mechanic.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.620
As you played through Dark Souls III,

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.340
I'm sure you noticed that you randomly get

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.880
an extra Estus sometimes, when you kill an enemy, right?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.460
Sometimes you even get two flasks,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.620
myself and Illusory* Wall who is a Dark Souls wizard,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.700
we set out to figure out exactly

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.040
what triggers this

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.340
to happen sometimes

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:36.840
and

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.360
so far, all we've discovered

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.900
is that certain enemies have a higher chance

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.840
to give you flasks than others,

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.180
enemies, like Dark Wraiths, for example,

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.500
they always give you two

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.060
and Red Eye Skeletons, ecetera.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:50.400
The odd thing is, though,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.360
even these enemies stopped giving us flasks after a little while.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.060
And a similar mechanic

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:57.600
in Dark Souls I

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.680
with Humanity.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.620
Enemies had a hidden point system

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.140
associated with them,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.740
which upon death would count towards you eventually

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.140
receiving a Humanity, guaranteed.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.960
And I have a theory

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.480
that Dark Souls III does work similar to this,

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.040
but I also have a faint hope

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.140
that the chance of you getting Estus

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.880
could be associated with the Luck stat.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.500
